Error [E2305]: This view points into `identity`, which this function owns
  --> tests/ui/vault_key_unlock_outlives_owner.jet:10:12
    |
 10 |     return unlock
    |            ^^^^^^
 Why: `identity` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: Return an owned copy with `place.copy()` (for example `value[a..b].copy()`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305
